# Reviewed sites of scripts/ct_scan.py: conditional branches and IT blocks
# that sit in assembly or that the compiler introduced on a line without a
# C condition, and C conditions that test_ct never executes (so TIMECOP
# never saw them, see scripts/ct_cover.py). Each one tests a public value.
# Format: function|file:line|reason
#
# SHAKE / Keccak: input and output lengths and offsets are public.
KeccakF1600_StateExtractBytes|keccakf1600.S:992|length (public)
KeccakF1600_StateExtractBytes|keccakf1600.S:997|offset within the lane (public)
KeccakF1600_StateExtractBytes|keccakf1600.S:1001|bytes left in the lane (public)
KeccakF1600_StateXORBytes|keccakf1600.S:888|length (public)
KeccakF1600_StateXORBytes|keccakf1600.S:893|offset within the lane (public)
KeccakF1600_StateXORBytes|keccakf1600.S:897|bytes left in the lane (public)
fndsa_sha3_extract_rate136|sha3_huang_cm4.s:84|lane counter (public)
# Pornin's sha3_cm4.s (the original-SHAKE build): length, destination
# alignment and the rate r of the SHAKE/SHA3 variant.
